{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory has no responsibility-chain error: the doctor actively queried the workspace, distinguished pending pathology/staging from treatment decisions, clarified entecavir versus inpatient orders, set hematology/original-team follow-up responsibilities, escalated post-chemotherapy oliguria/weakness to same-day in-person care, and repeatedly obtained caregiver receipts. Several high-order points were actively completed with meaningful impact, especially reprioritizing from routine follow-up to urgent assessment and repairing the result/follow-up responsibility chain. Closure is a safe valid open transition because the patient remains under in-person observation with clear next questions, responsible teams, medication boundaries, and return precautions.",
